{"name":"Gooseberry Fool","hex":"#acb75f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gooseberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fruit of species Ribes uva-crispa, related to the currant.","Any other plant or fruit in the subgenus Grossularia, distinguished from currants by bearing spines, including Ribes hirtellum (American gooseberry)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gooseberry"},{"term":"fool","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person with poor judgment or little intelligence.","A jester; a person whose role was to entertain a sovereign and the court (or lower personages)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To trick; to deceive.","To act in an idiotic manner; to act foolishly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fool"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fruit fool","blocks":[{"text":"A fool is an English dessert. Traditionally, fruit fool is made by folding puréed stewed fruit into sweet custard. Modern fool recipes often use whipped cream instead of custard. Additionally, a flavouring such as rose water may be added."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Raspberry_fool.jpg/330px-Raspberry_fool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit_fool","wikidata":"Q971054"},{"title":"Gooseberry","blocks":[{"text":"Gooseberry is a common name for many species of Ribes, as well as a large number of plants of similar appearance, and also several unrelated plants. The term gooseberry has a debated etymology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Stachelbeeren.jpg/330px-Stachelbeeren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gooseberry","wikidata":"Q17638951"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Blackberry_fool.JPG/500px-Blackberry_fool.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca